IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgk-part9-declared`
IMPORT `sgk-part9-ownership`

-- Tests for ss 243 to 246. Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion.

§ `Section 243`

-- (1): "Where it appears to the Minister that there is good reason to do so, the Minister may appoint".
#ASSERT `s 243(1) the Minister may appoint inspectors to investigate the ownership of the corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(1) the Minister may appoint inspectors to investigate the ownership of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the appointment "may define the scope".
#ASSERT `s 243(2) the appointment may define the scope of the inspector's investigation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(2) the appointment may define the scope of the inspector's investigation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): "the Minister must appoint an inspector ... unless the Minister is satisfied that the application is vexatious". Arguments: the application by members; the threshold of section 232 reached; vexatious.
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- vexatious
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE       -- not made by members
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE       -- the threshold is not reached
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 243(3) the Minister must appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister` DOES `s 243(3) appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation` AT 30
-- (3), second limb: "must not exclude ... except insofar as the Minister is satisfied that it is unreasonable". Arguments: application by members; the threshold; the application seeks the matter; unreasonable.
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the appointment must not exclude the matter from the scope of the investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the appointment must not exclude the matter from the scope of the investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the appointment must not exclude the matter from the scope of the investigation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the appointment must not exclude the matter from the scope of the investigation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 243(3) the appointment must not exclude the matter from the scope of the investigation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): "Subject to the terms of an inspector's appointment, the inspector's powers extend to the investigation of any circumstances suggesting the existence of an arrangement or understanding". Arguments: excluded by the terms; suggests an arrangement; relevant.
#ASSERT `s 243(4) the inspector's powers extend to the investigation of the circumstances` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(4) the inspector's powers extend to the investigation of the circumstances` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 243(4) the inspector's powers extend to the investigation of the circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243(4) the inspector's powers extend to the investigation of the circumstances` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243(4) the inspector's powers extend to the investigation of the circumstances` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5).
#ASSERT `s 243(5) the provisions of Part 9 on the investigation of declared companies apply to the investigation with the necessary modifications` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(5) the provisions of Part 9 on the investigation of declared companies apply to the investigation with the necessary modifications` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)(a). Arguments: an investigation under section 243; financially interested; able to control or influence; the inspector has reasonable cause to believe.
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(a) Part 9 applies in relation to the person as it applies in relation to officers and agents of the corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(a) Part 9 applies in relation to the person as it applies in relation to officers and agents of the corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(a) Part 9 applies in relation to the person as it applies in relation to officers and agents of the corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(a) Part 9 applies in relation to the person as it applies in relation to officers and agents of the corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(a) Part 9 applies in relation to the person as it applies in relation to officers and agents of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)(b). Arguments: an investigation under section 243; the Minister's opinion / the Minister thinks fit; the parts.
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(b) the Minister is not bound to furnish the person with a copy of the report or with a complete copy of it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(b) the Minister is not bound to furnish the person with a copy of the report or with a complete copy of it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(b) the Minister is not bound to furnish the person with a copy of the report or with a complete copy of it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(b) the Minister may cause a copy of the report or of the parts of it to be kept by the Registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(b) the Minister may cause a copy of the report or of the parts of it to be kept by the Registrar` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(b) the Minister may cause a copy of the report or of the parts of it to be kept by the Registrar` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243(5)(b) the Minister may cause a copy of the report or of the parts of it to be kept by the Registrar` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 244`

-- (1): "Where it appears to the Minister that there is good reason ... and that it is unnecessary to appoint an inspector ..., the Minister may require any person whom the Minister has reasonable cause to believe".
#ASSERT `s 244(1) the Minister may require the person to give the information to the Minister` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(1) the Minister may require the person to give the information to the Minister` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 244(1) the Minister may require the person to give the information to the Minister` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- an inspector is necessary
#ASSERT `s 244(1) the Minister may require the person to give the information to the Minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- no reasonable cause to believe the person has the information
-- (2): "deemed to have an interest" in three cases.
#ASSERT `s 244(2) the person is deemed to have an interest in the share or debenture for the purposes of section 244` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(2) the person is deemed to have an interest in the share or debenture for the purposes of section 244` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(2) the person is deemed to have an interest in the share or debenture for the purposes of section 244` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(2) the person is deemed to have an interest in the share or debenture for the purposes of section 244` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the offence, "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both". Arguments: fails to give; knowingly false; recklessly false.
#ASSERT `s 244(3) the person is guilty of the offence of failing to give information or giving false information` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(3) the person is guilty of the offence of failing to give information or giving false information` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(3) the person is guilty of the offence of failing to give information or giving false information` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(3) the person is guilty of the offence of failing to give information or giving false information` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 244(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 244(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 244(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 244(3) a person must give the information required of the person under section 244` "A. Tan" 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 244(3) a person must give the information required of the person under section 244` "A. Tan" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 244(3) give the Minister information required under section 244` AT 10
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 244(3) a person must not make a statement to the Minister that the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly make one` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 244(3) make to the Minister a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly makes a statement false in a material particular` AT 4
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 244(3) a person must not make a statement to the Minister that the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly make one` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
-- (4): "This section applies to a banking corporation but nothing therein requires, subject to the provisions of the Banking Act 1970, disclosure by a banking corporation ... of any information as to the affairs of any of its customers other than the corporation of which it is the banker". Arguments: banking corporation; a customer's information; the Banking Act provides otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 244(4) section 244 applies to the banking corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(4) section 244 applies to the banking corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 244(4) section 244 requires the banking corporation to disclose the information to the Minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 244(4) section 244 requires the banking corporation to disclose the information to the Minister` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the Banking Act is outside the text
#ASSERT `s 244(4) section 244 requires the banking corporation to disclose the information to the Minister` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 244(4) section 244 requires the banking corporation to disclose the information to the Minister` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5), (6), (7).
#ASSERT `s 244(5) the Minister may delegate the powers under section 244 to the delegate` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(5) the Minister may delegate the powers under section 244 to the delegate` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(5) the Minister may delegate the powers under section 244 to the delegate` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- not by notification in the Gazette
#ASSERT `s 244(5) the Minister may delegate the powers under section 244 to the delegate` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- not one of the two kinds of delegate
#ASSERT `s 244(6) the committee or body must keep the Minister informed of any information obtained under section 244` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(6) the committee or body must keep the Minister informed of any information obtained under section 244` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 244(6) the committee or body must keep the Minister informed of any information obtained under section 244` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 244(7) the Minister may exercise the power despite a delegation of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 244(7) the Minister may exercise the power despite a delegation of it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 245`

-- (1): "Where ... it appears to the Minister that there is difficulty in finding out the relevant facts ..., the Minister may by order in the Gazette direct".
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the Minister may by order in the Gazette direct that the shares are until further order subject to the restrictions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the Minister may by order in the Gazette direct that the shares are until further order subject to the restrictions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The four restrictions. Arguments: subject to an order; the act; the company is in liquidation.
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` TRUE `s 245(1)(a) a transfer of the shares, an exercise of the right to acquire or dispose of the shares, or (for unissued shares) a transfer of the right to be issued with them or an issue of them` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` TRUE `s 245(1)(b) an exercise of voting rights in respect of the shares` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` TRUE `s 245(1)(c) an issue of further shares in right of the shares or pursuant to an offer made to the holder` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` TRUE `s 245(1)(d) a payment of sums due from the company on the shares, whether in respect of capital or otherwise` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` TRUE `s 245(1)(d) a payment of sums due from the company on the shares, whether in respect of capital or otherwise` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "except in a liquidation"
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` TRUE `s 245(1)(a) a transfer of the shares, an exercise of the right to acquire or dispose of the shares, or (for unissued shares) a transfer of the right to be issued with them or an issue of them` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- a liquidation excuses only the payment
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` TRUE `s 245(1) any other act concerning the shares` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the act is void or barred by the restrictions` FALSE `s 245(1)(a) a transfer of the shares, an exercise of the right to acquire or dispose of the shares, or (for unissued shares) a transfer of the right to be issued with them or an issue of them` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2). Arguments: the order lifts the restrictions; expressed to permit a transfer; the right or offer is earlier than the transfer.
#ASSERT `s 245(2) the order may continue the application of subsection (1)(c) and (d) to the shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(2) the order may continue the application of subsection (1)(c) and (d) to the shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 245(2) the order may continue the application of subsection (1)(c) and (d) to the shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 245(2) the order may continue the application of subsection (1)(c) and (d) to the shares` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): arguments: subject to the restrictions; knowledge; exercises or purports to exercise a right; votes or appoints a proxy; holder; fails to notify.
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- (a) needs knowledge
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- knowledge alone is not enough
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- (b) needs no knowledge
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- a holder who did notify
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- not a holder
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the person is guilty of the offence of dealing in shares subject to the restrictions` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- the shares are not subject to the restrictions
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 245(3)(a) a person must not exercise a right to dispose of shares subject to the restrictions, or a right to be issued with them, knowing of the restrictions` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 245(3) exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of shares, or a right to be issued with shares, knowing they are subject to the restrictions` AT 6
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 245(3)(a) a person must not exercise a right to dispose of shares subject to the restrictions, or a right to be issued with them, knowing of the restrictions` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 245(3)(b) a person must not vote in respect of shares subject to the restrictions or appoint a proxy to vote` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 245(3) vote in respect of shares subject to the restrictions, or appoint a proxy to vote` AT 6
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 245(3)(b) a person must not vote in respect of shares subject to the restrictions or appoint a proxy to vote` "A. Tan" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 245(3)(c) the holder must notify the persons entitled to vote of the restrictions` "A. Tan" 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 245(3)(c) the holder must notify the persons entitled to vote of the restrictions` "A. Tan" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a person` "A. Tan" DOES `s 245(3) notify the holders entitled to vote of the restrictions` AT 6
-- (4): the officer in default and the company; "or", not "both".
#ASSERT `s 245(4) the officer is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(4) the officer is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- an officer not in default
#ASSERT `s 245(4) the officer is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- no shares issued in contravention
#ASSERT `s 245(4) the company is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(4) the company is guilty of the offence of issuing shares in contravention of the restrictions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 245(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 245(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 245(4) the company must not issue shares in contravention of the restrictions` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 231 a company` "Acme Ltd" DOES `s 245(4) issue shares in contravention of the restrictions` AT 6
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 245(4) the company must not issue shares in contravention of the restrictions` "Acme Ltd" AT 0 WITH
-- (5): "A prosecution must not be instituted under this section except with the consent of the Public Prosecutor".
#ASSERT `s 245(5) the prosecution is barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(5) the prosecution is barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 245(5) the prosecution is barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 245(5) the prosecution is barred for want of the consent of the Public Prosecutor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6).
#ASSERT `s 245(6) section 245 applies to the debentures as it applies to shares` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(6) section 245 applies to the debentures as it applies to shares` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 246`

#ASSERT `s 246 the Minister may by notice declare that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as an inspector appointed under section 231` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246 the Minister may by notice declare that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as an inspector appointed under section 231` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 246 the Minister may by notice declare that the inspector is to have the same powers and duties in Singapore as an inspector appointed under section 231` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 246 the inspector has the powers and duties of an inspector appointed under section 231` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246 the inspector has the powers and duties of an inspector appointed under section 231` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
